      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{600bb08cb76d6f78b108fb38|full_name}: I can see now how bad it also might be for regular players, there comes a point where accepting a friend request can be a result of a form of peer pressure or harassment. Nobody should feel forced into these awkward social situations where they're feeling pressured to be friends with someone they don't want to be friends with. \n\nThese are one of the rare cases where using moderation like blocking and muting can be quite a difficult call for the individual being harassed as well. Since often these forms of predatory forced friend requests make the victim feel obligated to \"be nice\" and not say no or decline in a way that shows their true feelings.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
