  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-01-18T20:36:57.197Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Please listen to your top creators and add a toggle to turn off friend requests. \n\nMany others have echoed the same sentiment that having excessive friend requests from new users ruins the experience for top creators on the platform. Often receiving friend requests with offensive / gore / pornographic avatar thumbnails in the request, or racist or offensive names. \n\nWhy is there still no option for us to disable the ability for people to send us friend requests? I take a 1 month break and sometimes come back to so much spam that it nearly crashes my game every time I open the social list. \n\nI hope my frustration doesn't come off as aggression here, but it's very demotivating creating content for a platform that won't consider basic features to protect creators from unwanted spam. Especially since some of the subject matter explained earlier is quite traumatic and is abused a lot with friend requests.",
